cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these maps or the code, please cite them as below, together with the input data listed in the README."
title: "Lower limit of brittle seismicity beneath the Japanese islands (based on JMA unified catalogue 2001-2024)"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Ikegami
    given-names: Fumihiko
    affiliation: Ikegami GeoResearch
repository-code: "https://github.com/geoign/JMA_seismogenic_bottom_2001-2024"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-23"
abstract: >-
  Maps of the lower limit of brittle (ordinary) seismicity beneath the Japanese islands on
  0.1-degree and 0.025-degree nodes, from upper-plate hypocentres of the JMA unified catalogue
  2001-2024. At every node a soft-bottomed depth distribution is fitted by weighted maximum
  likelihood, with aftershock sequences down-weighted by nearest-neighbour declustering. The
  primary product D_b10 is the depth at which the modelled brittle rate falls to 10 percent, a
  model-based counterpart of D90. The code is under the MIT licence. This is an independent work
  by the author, not a product of the Japan Meteorological Agency.
keywords:
  - seismogenic zone
  - brittle-ductile transition
  - D90
  - JMA unified hypocenter catalogue
  - declustering
  - Japan
